.Dd March 1, 2026
.Dt SIZE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm size
.Nd report section sizes for ELF objects and archives
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl A | Fl B | Fl -format Ns = Ns Cm sysv | berkeley | gnu
.Op Fl d | Fl o | Fl x | Fl -radix Ns = Ns Cm 8 | 10 | 16
.Op Fl t | Fl -totals
.Op Fl -common
.Op Fl -target Ns = Ns Ar bfdname
.Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints size accounting for ELF input files.
By default it emits Berkeley-style output with
text, data, bss, decimal total, and hexadecimal total columns.
Archive input
.Pq Pa .a
is traversed per member and printed as
.Li archive(member) .
Thin archives are resolved from filesystem member paths.
.Pp
The command supports Berkeley, SysV, and GNU display styles and can apply
radix formatting to all numeric columns.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--format=berkeley"
.It Fl A , Fl -format=sysv
Use SysV output format with per-section tables.
.It Fl B , Fl -format=berkeley
Use Berkeley output format (default).
.It Fl -format=gnu
Use GNU output format.
.It Fl d , Fl -radix=10
Format numeric output in decimal.
.It Fl o , Fl -radix=8
Format numeric output in octal.
.It Fl x , Fl -radix=16
Format numeric output in hexadecimal.
.It Fl t , Fl -totals
Force printing a grand total row/table.
For multiple inputs, totals are printed by default.
.It Fl -common
Include
.Dv SHN_COMMON
symbol sizes in the bss total.
.It Fl -target= Ns Ar bfdname
Accepted for GNU compatibility and ignored.
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print version information and exit.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show usage and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
Returns 0 on success.
Returns 1 if any input file fails to process.
Non-ELF top-level inputs are reported as file format not recognized.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Berkeley format (default)
.Dl size foo.o bar.o
.It SysV per-section output
.Dl size -A libfoo.a
.It GNU format with hexadecimal radix
.Dl size --format=gnu -x foo.o
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ar 1 ,
.Xr readelf 1 ,
.Xr objdump 1 ,
.Xr elfobj 3
